{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>Her sons rose</b> — in the morning, for her lamp did not go out at night." "<b>and they praise her</b> — this is the praise that they say to her: <b>Many daughters have done valor</b> — they have acquired wealth." "<b>You have excelled</b> — like \"and one of its young lions arose\" (Ezekiel 19:6), that is, she has grown great above all of them."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {2 "Ibn Ezra cites Ezekiel 19:6 (וַתַּעַל אַחַת מִגּוֹרְתֶּיהָ) as a parallel for the root עלה meaning 'to rise/excel'; the parenthetical gloss clarifies this is his illustration."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:55.903490095Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}